    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Traditional recipes use preserved lemon, which is salted and fermented for weeks. Fresh lemon sliced thin and added early in the braise gives a good approximation. If you have preserved lemon, use a quarter of it rinsed and finely chopped in place of the two fresh lemons." }]
      },
